<article class="env-lemma" id="0E23">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0E23">Lemma <span data-tag="0E23">36.22.9</span>.</a> Consider a cartesian diagram of schemes </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ Z' \ar[r]_{i'} \ar[d]_ g &  X' \ar[d]^ f \\  Z \ar[r]^ i &  X }  \]
</div>
  <p> where $i$ is a closed immersion. If $Z$ and $X'$ are tor independent over $X$, then $Ri'_* \circ Lg^* = Lf^* \circ Ri_*$ as functors $D(\mathcal{O}_ Z) \to D(\mathcal{O}_{X'})$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Note that the lemma is supposed to hold for all $K \in D(\mathcal{O}_ Z)$. Observe that $i_*$ and $i'_*$ are exact functors and hence $Ri_*$ and $Ri'_*$ are computed by applying $i_*$ and $i'_*$ to any representatives. Thus the base change map 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  Lf^*(Ri_*(K)) \longrightarrow Ri'_*(Lg^*(K))  \]
</div>
    <p>
       on stalks at a point $z' \in Z'$ with image $z \in Z$ is given by 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  K_ z \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_{X, z}}^\mathbf {L} \mathcal{O}_{X', z'} \longrightarrow K_ z \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_{Z, z}}^\mathbf {L} \mathcal{O}_{Z', z'}  \]
</div>
    <p>
       This map is an isomorphism by More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0661" data-tag="0661">15.62.2</a> and the assumed tor independence. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>